# All That Glitters counts the artifacts and enchantments its controller has, the Aura itself included, and not an
# opponent's. Bot1 enchants its own Ornithopter (an artifact creature) with Sol Ring out: Ornithopter, Sol Ring and the
# Aura make 3, so a 0/2 is 3/5, though Bot2 has a Sol Ring of its own. Before any creature exists the Aura cannot be
# cast (it enchants a creature: CR 303.4a), and Bot2's Disenchant on Bot1's Sol Ring drops the bonus to 2 (CR 613.4c).

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Sol Ring
Ornithopter
All That Glitters
Plains
Plains
Plains
Plains x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Sol Ring
Disenchant
Plains
Plains
Plains
Plains
Plains x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
! Bot1.Hand.All That Glitters.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.All That Glitters.Cast(Ornithopter)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = 3
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Toughness = 5
? Bot1.Battlefield.All That Glitters.AttachedTo = Ornithopter
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains#2.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Disenchant.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring)
[T4 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Toughness = 4
Bot1.Graveyard = Sol Ring
Bot2.Battlefield.Sol Ring.Tapped = false
